Z||000000||jerpro||05-30-2001||03:14 PM||||I am planning on transforming my garage into a fully operational paint shop and am going to paint my car bluemetallic (camaro style) with white lettering and white paint strips on top.<BR>does anyone know how to paint the strips on top? or ar they stick ons? I have no idea.||||reg||1
Z||000001||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||04:16 PM||||I am not sure where, but a friend bought a stencil set for his corvette. just tape on,(they had double sided tape around the edges) tape over all areas around hood roof, and trunk. and shoot it. I think they do have stick ons too, but I wouldn't go that route if I had a paint booth.||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||05-30-2001||04:18 PM||||There are stickons but they look like sh1t do'nt do it, paint it.. spend the time||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-30-2001||10:44 PM||||I saw a stick on set of decals on a 70's challenger the other day.  The design covered about 70% of the hood.  It looked pretty crappy IMO, and there were some bubbles too.<P>The decals are the easy way out.  Go the stencil route, pay the extra money for a little bit more paint, and make it look right the first time.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
